      "description": "Fatbeam is a Coeur d'Alene, Idaho-based owner-operator of fiber networks serving commercial, education, healthcare, government, carrier, tower, residential and multifamily customers across Arizona, Idaho, Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, Oregon, Washington and Wyoming. Its services include dedicated internet access, Ethernet private line, wavelength, dark fiber, wireless backup, tower and data-center connectivity, managed Wi-Fi, cyber/cloud and residential fiber/wireless. Fatbeam's current network page reports 1,600+ on-net buildings, 150,000+ total fiber miles and 150+ cities across eight states; Basalt's current portfolio page reports 1,250 route miles. A June 2023 regulator filing separately reported 1,252 route miles, 13 metro markets, 128,000+ strand miles and over 40 cities. Basalt IV announced an agreement to acquire Fatbeam on March 27, 2023, and Project Lighthouse AIV Feeder LP acquired all Fatbeam Holdings interests effective May 31, 2023. Fatbeam remains in Basalt's current portfolio, and no later ownership transfer or signed pending exit was identified through August 18, 2026.",
